# Stand-in actors for the mainnet activation rehearsal. FORK ONLY: these addresses have no keys. Each is the last 20
# bytes of keccak256("lm-mainnet-fork:<role>") (unused on Ethereum and BSC, nonce 0), and anvil (--auto-impersonate)
# sends their transactions. The real legacy multisig and its owners are impersonated at their live addresses.
DEPLOYER=${MAINNET_DEPLOYER:-0xD26A732D1fDac09f4ED7b6cfe0dec234e39604cB} # deployer: runs script/Deploy.s.sol; set MAINNET_DEPLOYER to the real deployer to predict the mainnet addresses
GOV_OWNER=0x2F19980DF27d2237EE83cfd8D69B19d195113f87      # governance-owner: sole owner of the 1-of-1 Governance Safe stand-in
GUARDIAN_OWNER=0x6648F274AE7b1a8f82c2258395fF8192651214Eb # guardian-owner: sole owner of the 1-of-1 Guardian Safe stand-in
FUNDING_OP=0xBA21033bd948f8E7947Aa85B27d58bAf74a36163     # funding-operator
RECALL_OP=0x6418ffF2D0209C5ed9C748d32a08E57d09892278      # recall-operator
RESERVE_WALLET=0x7b872e2D09633316951a992e2a444512D85DC0EA # reserve-wallet: simulated reserve holder (used when RESERVE_WALLETS is empty)
BRIDGE_USER=0xB86306814f136B8898c6d4b8799C3AF85f8f1eda    # bridge-user: receiver/sender of the simulated CCIP round trip
ATTACKER=0xf2c9BC2643d15750206F736Ae1c3A52F730933f2       # destination of the malicious proposal the Guardian cancels
